.TH "OSTRYA\-SEND" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-send \- Serve one pull session over standard input and standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya send [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve one pull session over standard input and standard output.
.PP
An ssh pull runs this command on the remote side. The command answers each \fB\%Get\fR path as the archive view of \fB\%ostrya serve\fR answers a \fB\%GET\fR of that path. It takes no lock and writes no file in the repository.
.PP
The client name is \%\-\-client, else the value of \fB\%LOGNAME\fR, which sshd sets from the password entry of the user. With neither, the command writes an error line and exits \%1 before it opens the repository. The name does not limit the paths that the session serves.
.PP
Standard output carries the frames of the session alone. On failure, the command writes \fB\%error: MESSAGE\fR to standard error. It writes nothing else, also under \%\-\-verbose. It exits \%0 when standard input ends at a frame boundary, and \%1 after an \fB\%Error\fR frame or a failed write.
.PP
An \fB\%authorized_keys\fR entry with \fB\%command="ostrya send \-\-repo=PATH"\fR limits an ssh key to a pull from one repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-client\fR \fINAME\fR
The client name of the session, in place of \fB\%LOGNAME\fR\&.
.IP
The name does not limit the paths that the session serves. The option is safe only under a forced \fB\%command=\fR in \fB\%authorized_keys\fR, because a user with a shell can give any name.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
